{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00481",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.02,
      "end_seconds": 5.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "Come in, come in. Pull the door closed behind you, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 5.72,
      "end_seconds": 6.42,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Hi."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.2,
      "end_seconds": 10.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Okay, tell me from the beginning, what's been happening?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.69,
      "end_seconds": 19.46,
      "duration_seconds": 7.77,
      "text": "Doctor, it's an itchy rash. It's getting on my nerves now. I took the morning off to come in today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.26,
      "end_seconds": 22.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "When did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.17,
      "end_seconds": 33.05,
      "duration_seconds": 9.88,
      "text": "Yeah, it's been going on for five days. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.94,
      "end_seconds": 43.76,
      "duration_seconds": 9.82,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps. I ask because it helps me narrow things down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.76,
      "end_seconds": 57.5,
      "duration_seconds": 12.74,
      "text": "It's a few times a day. Only moisturiser, and it's not much. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.04,
      "end_seconds": 61.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.11,
      "end_seconds": 79.98,
      "duration_seconds": 16.87,
      "text": "Well, when it starts I tend to get cracked skin on my hands as well. As for cracked skin on my hands, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.81,
      "end_seconds": 85.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "Give me a second, I'm just scrolling back through your chart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.42,
      "end_seconds": 86.21,
      "duration_seconds": 0.79,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.56,
      "end_seconds": 99.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Have you had any oozing or joint pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.17,
      "end_seconds": 102.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "No, no oozing or joint pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 103.51,
      "end_seconds": 109.18,
      "duration_seconds": 5.67,
      "text": "Have you had any similar rash in family members, new soap or detergent or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.97,
      "end_seconds": 118.84,
      "duration_seconds": 5.87,
      "text": "No similar rash in family members, new soap or detergent or fever, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.49,
      "end_seconds": 122.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Alright, anything with your nerves, like weakness or numbness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.86,
      "end_seconds": 125.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.64,
      "end_seconds": 141.75,
      "duration_seconds": 15.11,
      "text": "I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.2,
      "end_seconds": 144.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "Thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 145.44,
      "end_seconds": 153.9,
      "duration_seconds": 8.46,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Pulse is 76 beats a minute, respiratory rate 18. Pressure 126 over 71, oxygen saturation is 98 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.38,
      "end_seconds": 172.53,
      "duration_seconds": 17.15,
      "text": "Good, thank you. What I'm doing here is putting together three things: what you tell me, what I find when I examine you, and what the tests show. None of those alone is enough, which is why we sometimes need to wait for results before being certain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.4,
      "end_seconds": 178.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Right, I appreciate you explaining that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.25,
      "end_seconds": 181.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Are you on any tablets or medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.04,
      "end_seconds": 190.01,
      "duration_seconds": 6.97,
      "text": "Hydrocortisone cream. I take it when needed for the eczema. It's Seretide inhaler, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.31,
      "end_seconds": 194.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Okay, I'm following. Has anything about your daily routine changed lately?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.91,
      "end_seconds": 210.87,
      "duration_seconds": 15.96,
      "text": "Not really, the days are pretty much the same, work and home, and I've been trying to fit appointments in around my schedule, which isn't always easy, so I'm glad we could find a time today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.26,
      "end_seconds": 214.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Okay, have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.99,
      "end_seconds": 216.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.21,
      "text": "No operations, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.25,
      "end_seconds": 224.27,
      "duration_seconds": 7.02,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for? These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 228.06,
      "end_seconds": 237.68,
      "duration_seconds": 9.62,
      "text": "I've had eczema for five years now. I did try to ignore it for a while. I've had asthma for about ten years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.39,
      "end_seconds": 246.72,
      "duration_seconds": 8.33,
      "text": "Okay, I'm following. Yes, I can see the eczema in your file as well. Anyone in the family with similar problems or other conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.14,
      "end_seconds": 250.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Um, um, my mother has diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.36,
      "end_seconds": 254.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Sorry about the noise outside, the building work never stops."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 255.56,
      "end_seconds": 257.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "I hadn't even noticed, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.19,
      "end_seconds": 269.03,
      "duration_seconds": 7.84,
      "text": "Right, do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all? I ask because it helps me narrow things down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 270.32,
      "end_seconds": 273.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Aspirin. I come out in... well, wheezing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.18,
      "end_seconds": 279.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "I'll examine you now, so please bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 280.75,
      "end_seconds": 281.45,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.57,
      "end_seconds": 284.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Alright, can you lie back for me?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.04,
      "end_seconds": 297.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "No signs of infection, no crusting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.38,
      "end_seconds": 301.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.99,
      "end_seconds": 304.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "I'll just check what's already recorded here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 305.02,
      "end_seconds": 305.92,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "Please do."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.03,
      "end_seconds": 345.63,
      "duration_seconds": 25.6,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. From what you've told me and what I found, this looks most like an eczema flare-up. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. I can't rule out contact dermatitis yet. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had an itchy rash for five days, and no joint pain or similar rash in family members."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 346.54,
      "end_seconds": 347.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.11,
      "end_seconds": 374.49,
      "duration_seconds": 26.38,
      "text": "I'm prescribing cetirizine, 10 milligrams, at night, for one week. That's for itching. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it. Let's use mometasone cream, once a day, for two weeks. That's for eczema. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well. Moisturise right after a bath, thick creams are better than lotions, and use a mild soap."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 375.73,
      "end_seconds": 391.49,
      "duration_seconds": 15.76,
      "text": "Try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit. Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 391.96,
      "end_seconds": 398.47,
      "duration_seconds": 6.51,
      "text": "Right. I want you to come back or go to emergency straight away if the symptoms get worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 399.56,
      "end_seconds": 401.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Yes, I'll do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 402.61,
      "end_seconds": 404.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "Come back in three weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 404.62,
      "end_seconds": 407.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "Okay, um, I'll book that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 407.85,
      "end_seconds": 412.19,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "Can you run through the plan with me quickly, just to be certain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 413.6,
      "end_seconds": 422.73,
      "duration_seconds": 9.13,
      "text": "So, I take the cetirizine, 10 milligrams, at night and take the mometasone cream, once a day. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 423.1,
      "end_seconds": 427.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 428.52,
      "end_seconds": 431.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "Um, I appreciate your time, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 432.27,
      "end_seconds": 434.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Bye for now, look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}